  "security_implications": "This chunk directly composes the advance matrix (adv_matrix) for Creator, OwnerInt, and Owner stages by concatenating sensitive data: sw_binding (potentially secret), otp_device_id_i (device identity), lc_keymgr_div_i (lifecycle), rom_digest_i (digest), revision_seed, creator_seed, and owner_seed. The valid signals gate when this matrix is considered ready. A mis-assertion of any valid signal could allow usage of incomplete or stale secrets in key derivation. The adv_dvalid[Owner] is hardwired to 1, potentially causing the Owner stage to accept an invalid seed. The width truncation risk in AdvDataWidth could silently drop secret bits. All these could lead to key leakage or incorrect key material.",
